With the support area broken, the downward trend will continue.</p>]]></content:encoded></item><item><title>LINK 8H – Trendline Breakout Pulling Back Into Demand Zone</title><link>https://www.tradingview.com/chart/LINKUSDT/FwYEadHC-LINK-8H-Trendline-Breakout-Pulling-Back-Into-Demand-Zone/</link><description>LINK on the 8H timeframe is currently trading around 11.080 after breaking above the rising trendline resistance and spiking from the demand zone near 10.000–10.400 all the way to a high near 12.200 before pulling back, with price now back inside the demand zone as the first critical test of whether the breakout structure holds.

The chart shows a rising trendline originating from the late June low near 7.080, connecting the July 7 low near 7.600, the July 28 low near 8.200, and the August 12 touch near 8.300–8.400 before price broke sharply higher. That trendline held every significant low across two months and now sits near 9.000 as a secondary support floor well below current price. The demand zone near 10.000–10.400, visible as the highlighted purple box, formed during the consolidation between August 15 and August 21 just before the breakout candle pushed price from that zone to the high near 12.200. Price has now pulled back from the high and is sitting directly inside that demand zone, with the prior breakout level acting as the support test. The 11.200 horizontal has been a pivot through the post-spike consolidation and sits as the immediate resistance above current price.

The demand zone near 10.000–10.400 is the most structurally significant level on the current chart as it represents both the pre-breakout consolidation base and the first meaningful support following the pullback from the spike high, making it the defining level for the continuation of the breakout structure.

Key Levels To Watch
→ 12.000–12.200 Spike high, major resistance above
→ 11.600–11.800 Prior consolidation zone, resistance
→ 11.200–11.400 Horizontal pivot, current resistance
→ 10.000–10.400 Demand zone, current support test
→ 9.200–9.400 Secondary support below demand zone
→ 9.000–9.100 Rising trendline, dynamic support (climbing)
→ Below 8.400 Trendline breakdown, breakout structure at risk

A hold inside the demand zone near 10.000–10.400 and a recovery back above 11.200–11.400 would confirm the demand zone as active support and reopen a move toward 11.600–11.800 and a retest of the spike high near 12.000–12.200.

A confirmed 8H close below the demand zone near 10.000 would suggest the breakout is failing to hold its base, exposing price to a move toward the rising trendline near 9.000–9.100 and potentially below on a deeper correction.

Spike pulling back into the demand zone that launched the move, most important test since the 
breakout. Hold 10.000–10.400 → breakout intact, eyes on 11.200–12.200. Lose 10.000 → base broken, trendline near 9.000 next. Bias bullish above rising trendline. Shift only on confirmed close below demand zone.</description><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 19:39:42 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.tradingview.com/chart/LINKUSDT/FwYEadHC-LINK-8H-Trendline-Breakout-Pulling-Back-Into-Demand-Zone/</guid><content:encoded><![CDATA[
