Circle Internet Group (CRCL) reported earnings of $0.18 per share on revenue of $701.32 million for the second quarter ended June 2026. The consensus earnings estimate was $0.16 per share on revenue of $744.88 million. The Earnings Whisper number was $0.19 per share. The company missed expectations by 5.26% while revenue grew 6.57% on a year-over-year basis.

“If you could take what we think of as money, make it digital and available on the internet, then that would dramatically change the way we use money and open up opportunity around the world. That’s the idea behind Circle.”
Jeremy Allaire
CEO and Co-Founder, Circle

 Technical Read 
After reviewing the fundamentals and getting a sense of Circle Internet Group’s business, here is my view of the technical setup based on the daily chart.
 Pattern and Entry Plan 
CRCL appears to be forming a cup-with-handle pattern. I plan to set an alert for a break above the handle, which would serve as my early entry signal. This area may also allow for a tighter stop loss, placed just below the most recent low.
 Position Management 
If the stock then breaks through the confirmation area shown on the chart, I would look to add to the position. Assuming the trade continues to develop as planned, I would shift to a trailing stop strategy, using a decisive close below the 21-day EMA, shown in blue, as my signal to exit.

 Use Your Own Rules 
If this idea resonates with you, make it your own by applying your personal investing or trading rules. Ultimately, it is your capital at risk, so the setup should fit your plan, risk tolerance, and decision-making process.
</description><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 19:30:07 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.tradingview.com/chart/CRCL/tFBpDWne-CRCL-Forming-a-Cup-with-Handle-Pattern/</guid><content:encoded><![CDATA[
