Let me start with what the chart shows, not with what I think.

Bitcoin topped a bit above 125,000 in October 2025. 

Since then it has lost more than half of its value, with the lowest prints in July 2026 in the 57,000 area. Today it trades near 77,000, back above the 70,598 line I call the First Accumulation Zone.

Now the part you cannot see on this chart. I overlaid the last three Bitcoin cycles on the current one, each scaled to start at the same point. Same script, same dates aligned, no cherry picking. The picture is boring in the best possible way, but extremely useful.

 Where we are in the cycle 

In every previous cycle, the low came roughly one year after the top. Then the market stayed flat and ugly for several months. The real recovery only started in the year after that.

Translate that to today and you get this:

- The low should be forming in the second half of 2026. 
- That was my expectation since the top, and it is exactly where we are. 
- Then a boring stretch until 2027, and only then the next leg up.

So, a correction now would be healthy for BTC.

And... the low is in, and I buy now? Not so fast. The low  may  be in. Past cycles also show a second visit to the bottom area before the turn. That is why I keep three levels on the chart, not one.


 The three zones 

 70,598 is the First Accumulation Zone . Price is back above it. If it holds, this is the first sign that the structure has changed.
 
61,079 is the Buy Zone.  This is where the market spent the summer. If we go back there, it is not a failure of the thesis. It is the cycle doing what cycles do.

 53,195 is the Aggressive Buy . A drop below 57,000 would be a gift for a patient investor with a multi year horizon. It would not be comfortable.  Market gifts rarely are. 


 A smaller crash and a smaller boom 

Here is the objection I have heard most: previous bears cut Bitcoin by 70 to 80%. This one, so far, is around 55%. So either the crash is not finished, or something is different.

I think something is different, and it is good news. Bitcoin is a bigger and more mature asset than in 2018 or 2022. ETFs, institutions, more holders, less panic selling. A more mature asset moves less in both directions. The 80% crashes were the price of being small.

The same logic applies to the next rise. I do not expect a x20 like the old days. But look at what the cycle overlay says. Even the weakest of the previous three cycles multiplied its price several times from the low. A x2 or x3 over the next few years would already be the "mature" version of that story, and the chart does not need anything heroic for it to happen.

A reward of at least 2-3 times the risk is a great trade for me, so I've been accumulating patiently for the last months and I'll do so in the upcoming months if the price go to the expected supports.



We will see if this cycle runs ahead of the previous ones or not. Either way, the plan is the same: buy in the zones, wait, and let 2027 do the work.

By the way, the blue lines on this chart are two historical trendline breakouts found by my Trendline Breakouts indicator, with +80% and +48% peak gains after the break with just a 5% Stop Loss, you can find more info in my profile.</description><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 19:29:44 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.tradingview.com/chart/BTCUSD/PgzuvCz9-BTCUSD-the-bear-cycle-is-close-to-its-end-The-low-may-already/</guid><content:encoded><![CDATA[
