In this 1-Hour chart analysis for Gold, we are evaluating the price behavior following a firm bounce from the major support region.
Technical Breakdown:
Support Defense: Price successfully defended the 4,300 Support Zone, indicating significant buying interest and structural rejection at lower levels.
Channel Exit: Gold has broken out of its downward corrective channel, moving past earlier CHoCH levels and leaving an overhead FVG area behind.
Current Action: Price is currently trading around 4,374, establishing momentum above the immediate support zone.
Key Technical Levels:
Support Zone: 4,300 – 4,320
Major Resistance / Target Zone: 4,680 – 4,700
Mid-Range Zone: 4,500
Possible Pathways:
Direct Path: A continuous higher-high structure toward the 4,700 resistance zone with minor pullbacks along the way.
Deeper Retest Path: A temporary pullback/consolidation toward mid-support before building enough momentum for a secondary rally toward 4,700.
Risk management is essential—always confirm setups on lower timeframes before taking action.
Disclaimer:
This analysis is strictly for educational and market tracking purposes. It does not constitute financial or trading advice. Always perform your own research and manage risk responsibly.</description><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 18:55:06 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.tradingview.com/chart/GOLD/cpKmyLzn-Support-Bounce-are-Dual-Outlook-Scenarios/</guid><content:encoded><![CDATA[
